<title>EGYPT: Egypt exports 45,193 T cotton this season-trade.</title>
<headline>Egypt exports 45,193 T cotton this season-trade.</headline>
<dateline>CAIRO 1996-11-18</dateline>
<text>
<p>Egypt has sold 45,193 tonnes of cotton for export so far this season, the Alexandria Cotton Exporters Association (Alcotexa) said on Monday.</p>
<p>Egypt had expected to export between 125,000 and 150,000 tonnes of this year's harvest but the latest figures suggested that demand was slackening.</p>
<p>In the ninth week of the marketing season exporters sold only 1,019 bales (333 tonnes), said Alcotexa, which coordinates prices and exports by both private and state-owned firms. The ninth week ended on November 16.</p>
<p>The biggest buyers this season have been in the United States (16,068 tonnes), Italy (6,052) and Japan (2,911). --Cairo newsroom +20 2 578 3290/1</p>
